{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py`, which drives report totals via `price_summary` in `repo/rows.py`.\n\n**Cause:** Amounts were floored to the lower nickel (`(cents // 5) * 5`) instead of rounding to the nearest 5¢. For example, 23¢ became 20¢ instead of 25¢, so line items and `rounded_total` in the report were systematically low whenever the remainder was 3 or 4 cents.\n\n**Change:** Use nearest-nickel rounding: `round(cents / 5) * 5`, matching the docstring (23 → 25, 22 → 20).\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_pricing.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"d727ad70-b916-4e35-88f1-17f22358faf3"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":21986,"duration_api_ms":21986,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for how report prices are rounded.\n\n\nIdentifying the bug: `round_to_nickel` floors to the lower nickel instead of rounding to the nearest 5 cents (23¢ → 20¢ instead of 25¢). Fixing it.\n\n\nThe issue was in `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py`, which drives report totals via `price_summary` in `repo/rows.py`.\n\n**Cause:** Amounts were floored to the lower nickel (`(cents // 5) * 5`) instead of rounding to the nearest 5¢. For example, 23¢ became 20¢ instead of 25¢, so line items and `rounded_total` in the report were systematically low whenever the remainder was 3 or 4 cents.\n\n**Change:** Use nearest-nickel rounding: `round(cents / 5) * 5`, matching the docstring (23 → 25, 22 → 20).\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_pricing.py` pass.","session_id":"d727ad70-b916-4e35-88f1-17f22358faf3","request_id":"eae290bc-3c60-4a03-a0c7-19a71fc8813d","usage":{"inputTokens":13673,"outputTokens":979,"cacheReadTokens":71456,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
